data: {"choices":[{"delta":{"tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"content\": \"# Plan — mission m1: greet, tested\\n\\nMission (from mission.md):\\n1. `src/greet.py` with `greet(name)` returning `\\\"Hello, \u003cname\u003e!\\\"`\\n2. `tests/test_greet.py` covering a normal name and the empty string\\n3. `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` exits 0\\n\\nRepo state: subject repo is at base (README only); both files must be created from scratch.\\n\\n## Allocation\\n- dev (owns the subject repo): implement both files, run the unittest command, commit to its own branch, reply honestly.\\n\\n## Judgment criteria (what I will verify by fetching dev's branch, not by trusting the report)\\n- `src/greet.py` exists and `greet(name)` returns exactly `\\\"Hello, \u003cname\u003e!\\\"`.\\n- `tests/test_greet.py` exists and covers: a normal name AND the empty string.\\n- `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` exits 0 in a fresh checkout of dev's branch.\\n\\n## Contingency\\n- If dev's first attempt fails judgment: send precise rework (what is wrong, what to change).\\n- Small mission: if it stalls, wrap up honestly with the appropriate non-met outcome rather than iterating forever.\\n\", \"filePath\": \"/home/<USER:1>/.local/share/cs-campaign/output/plan-m1.md\"}","name":"write"},"id":"write_12","index":0,"type":"function"}]},"finish_reason":null,"index":0,"raw_output":null}],"created":1787461601,"id":"chatcmpl-c68509ca98fa4ce491bbc88f46aa0f1e","model":"accounts/fireworks/models/kimi-k3","object":"chat.completion.chunk","usage":null}

